{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>had completed their circuit</b> — its meaning: when the cycle of the days of the week completed, for he had seven sons." "<b>perhaps</b> — like פן, a term of alarm and fear, 'perhaps such and such may happen.' Like it: 'Perhaps my father will depart from me' (Genesis 27:12), 'Perhaps the woman will not want' (Genesis 24:5)." "<b>and blessed</b> — a term of euphemism, and the reverse is like: 'Naboth has blessed Elohim and king' (1 Kings 21:13)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:29.796712375Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}